<title>ITALY: Olivetti details ex-Soviet Union credits.</title>
<headline>Olivetti details ex-Soviet Union credits.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian information technology group Olivetti said it had credits outstanding to the former Soviet Union of 134 billion lire in principal and 74 billion in interest.</p>
<p>Olivetti said in a statement issued in response to detailed questions from market regulator Consob that the credits arose from the supply of an automated plant for the production of numerically controlled instruments.</p>
<p>The plant was built in St Petersburg in 1989.</p>
</text>
